<title>JAPAN: TABLE-Japan June household spending down 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Japan June household spending down 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's household spending in June fell 4.7 percent in real terms from a year earlier to an average 310,990 yen per household, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The agency also said that household spending in the January-June period fell a real 0.2 percent from the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of year-on-year percentage changes in June and May in real and nominal terms:</p>
<p>					   June		 May</p>
<p>				     Real   Nominal    Real   Nominal</p>
<p>Overall household spending   -4.7    -2.5     -2.2    -0.3</p>
<p>(average 310,990 yen)</p>
<p>Spending by wage earners     -5.8    -3.6     -1.5    +0.4</p>
<p>(average 330,956 yen)</p>
</text>
